  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross border Peacebuilding and Conflict Transformation Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marsabit Interfaith Council (MIC) peacebuilding and conflict transformation was an initiative of the Diocese of Marsabit in late 2005 that brought together three faith families of Catholics, Protestants and the Muslims in Marsabit. MIC has over the years gained confidence and recognition of the communities and agencies (both governmental and non-governmental) in Marsabit with respect to their peacebuilding and conflict transformation activities. 

The interfaith peacebuilding and conflict transformation initiative has employed short, medium and long-term measures in addressing the conflicts in Marsabit. The medium term measures have included the development of strategies and interventions to promote and sustain the transition from violent conflict to sustainable development and to build &quot;fire walls&quot; that inhibit regular societal conflict from spiralling back into violence. These measures seek to encourage tolerance and understanding between different ethnic groups. They seek to address the emotive and attitudinal effects of conflicts by dissolving the hatred, suspicions, fears, anger, and hostility that can block individuals&apos; capacities to heal, forgive, and reconcile, as well as to find new solutions - non-violent ones - to old problems. Long-term measures take into account the structural causes of the inter-ethnic animosity.
 
This project seeks to build on the medium and long-term processes to transform the conflict and create opportunities for peacebuilding. It seeks to continue creating confidence among the communities by promoting forgiveness, dissolving hatred, anger and bringing about reconciliation. In doing this, the project bases its success on an ownership structure that the community itself can recognize and approve of which essentially led to the creation of the Marsabit Interfaith Council. 

The project&#x2019;s main goal is enhanced promotion of peace among the different communities in Marsabit region by encouraging tolerance, understanding and reconciliation. This is projected to be achieved through strengthening the capacity in terms of knowledge and skills of community and inter-faith leaders in conflict management and peacebuilding; promoting dialogue among the different communities residing in the District by engaging the local community and traditional leaders, women groups, youth groups, inter-faith leaders and cross-border community representatives; and increasing the level of networking with organizations and other agencies involved in peacebuilding and general development of the region. Over the last three years that interfaith peacebuilding and conflict transformation initiative has been implemented in Marsabit, there has been improved opportunity for active inter-religious dialogues and tolerance, as well as acceptance of the initiative by communities, governmental and other non-governmental agencies in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
